<title>NETHERLANDS: Volker Stevin shares leap on merger news.</title>
<headline>Volker Stevin shares leap on merger news.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch builder Volker Stevin NV surged more than six percent on news it was in merger talks with rival Kondor Wessels Groep NV.</p>
<p>The shares stood at 200.50 guilders at 0940 GMT, up 12.10 from the previous close, after earlier hitting a year high of 200.70.</p>
<p>Kondor Wessels' shares were 2.10 firmer at 88.80 after earlier touching 89.00, also a year high.</p>
<p>Earlier the companies said they were holding talks to merge, based on an expected exchange of 2.25 Kondor Wessels shares for one Volker Stevin share.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
